Hi mate,<br><br>Yes, the button on the front of the radio.  The UP button worked fine on the original firmware though...<br><br>Also, I noticed in the firmware info on my car radio, which is a Retevis RT90, cpu type is "STM".<br><br>This new radio is the TYT MD9600, I thought its meant to be the exact same radio.. and its cpu type is "TYT".<br><br>Could this be an issue?<br><br>If its a bad connection, would re-seating the ribbon cables fix it? Its not like the button isnt working, its just doing the same as the band/esc button rather than navigating up.<br><br>Is there anyway to re-map the buttons like you can in the stock firmware?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6558">VK2KLF</a> — Sun Jan 19, 2025 10:54 am</p><hr />
