		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4768&amp;p=35187#p35187"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hi all,<br><br>I have just got a second TYT9600 for my base station.<br><br>I have flashed the latest version of the V5 Firmware, everything works, my codeplug installs fine.  Radio TX and RX fine.  <br><br>One issue, on the radio itself, the "UP" Button does not fuction as up, it is the same as the band/esc button which takes you to VFO mode.<br><em class="text-italics">Note, I have also tried going back to older versions and this still happens.</em><br><br>Any reason why this would happen? Can I change the button assignments?<br><br>Thanks in advance for your help guys.<br><br>Regards<br><br>Sven VK2KLF  <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_ugeek.gif" width="17" height="18" alt=":ugeek:" title="Uber Geek"></div></blockquote>Do you mean the buttons on the front of the radio or the button on the mic ?<br><br>If pressing the Up button on the front of the radio is acting the same as ESC button, then it sounds like a hardware fault. Possibly a bad connection between the front panel and the main board<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sun Jan 19, 2025 2:32 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
